**Count `rdf:rest` traversal work across all heads.**

`observe` rejects more than `MAX_BINDINGS` immutable facts, so the input is bounded. But each head starts a fresh traversal. A shared branching or cyclic `rdf:rest` subgraph can be scanned once per head while emitting only one row per head, making total edge scans quadratic in the retained-fact bound. Counting popped nodes alone does not cap edge scans. Count both popped nodes and examined `rdf:rest` edges against one work budget.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
     let mut rows = Vec::new();
+    let mut work = 0usize;
     for &head in &cells {
         let mut seen = BTreeSet::from([head]);
         let mut pending = vec![head];
         while let Some(cell) = pending.pop() {
+            work += 1;
+            if work > MAX_BINDINGS {
+                return false;
+            }
             if cells.contains(cell) {
                 rows.push((head, cell));
                 if rows.len() > MAX_BINDINGS {
                     return false;
                 }
             }
             for &tail in next.get(cell).into_iter().flatten() {
+                work += 1;
+                if work > MAX_BINDINGS {
+                    return false;
+                }
                 if seen.insert(tail) {
